> **Farzana says:** "This is what I love about lab stones in white gold. The price difference between E and D is almost nothing — maybe $50-$100. But you're putting it in a metal that actually shows that difference. You're not wasting the color upgrade. In yellow gold I'd tell you to buy G. Here? Buy D and spend what you save somewhere else."

