## The Setting Stack for White Gold Radiant

A radiant cut works in almost any setting. The cut has cropped corners, so it doesn't need the specialized V-prongs required for marquise or pear shapes. Standard four-prong and six-prong settings hold it securely and let the stone breathe.

Below are 15 settings currently in certified market inventory — 10 in 14k white gold and 5 in platinum. The Ring From column uses [1ct E-VVS1 IGI lab at $867](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) as the baseline stone.

